MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Five defects from the critique pass, all of them "the code contradicts what it
says": Login rendered a position:fixed Telegram debug dump in production over
the header; AdBanner ignored ADS_ENABLED, so the documented kill switch left
the ad on and nothing was actually un-turn-off-able; the sticky day header used
bg-app, a utility that is never generated, so fixtures bled through the blur;
--stagger was written in eight files and consumed nowhere, so the documented
40ms list stagger never ran; and the fixed MatchDetail pick CTA sat on top of
the ad beneath it.

Two supporting fixes the above needed: declare __ADS_ENABLED__ in vite-env.d.ts
(it was defined by vite.config but never declared, so reading it would not have
typechecked), and correct .env.example, which still described a src/lib/ads.ts
gate and an index.html snippet that no longer exist.

Verified in the built artifact both ways: with ADS_ENABLED unset the A-ADS
iframe is tree-shaken out of the bundle entirely (no request is ever made), and
with ADS_ENABLED=true the ad chunk returns, while the debug dump stays absent
from production in both.

